\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Attack--defense pairing (P2 advisory vs.\ the D1 comment/docstring strip, AST-equivalence gated). Recall on the malicious subset; $+g/{-}l$ = restore-gain ($0{\to }1$) / restore-loss ($1{\to }0$) flips of D1 vs.\ the attack arm; $p$ = exact paired McNemar (P2 vs P2+D1), descriptive; FP = benign false positives (attack $\to $ defended). Realized subsets after the AST gate: 24 malicious + 14 benign per model (7 comment-only snippets excluded, disclosed; Fisher $p{=}.40$, no label bias). P0 and P2 arms are verified cache hits of the $n{=}100$ expansion; the attack-arm FP column is quoted from that expansion (this batch adds no benign P2 generations). One granite P2+D1 output was unparseable (disclosed; baseline-positive), hence recall over $23$ parsed.\relax }}{4}{table.caption.4}\protected@file@percent }
