\newlabel{tab:main}{{3}{5}{Corrected-baseline grid (registered before the run): twenty seeds, F1/AUC mean$\pm $std over seeds (population, $ddof{=}0$). Strong centralized = \texttt {lbfgs} LR on train-fit standardized features ($C$ by train-only 3-fold CV); FedAvg = converged local fit + size-weighted average; per-client-best is oracle per-sample routing (an upper bound, not a deployable system). Text block = stateless HashingVectorizer ($2^{18}$, $L_2$). \pmPzRuns \ runs, \texttt {mock=false}. \relax }{table.caption.5}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Corrected-baseline comparison (FedAvg $-$ strong centralized), paired per seed over 20 seeds, F1. \textbf  {TOST}: pre-registered equivalence margin $\pm .02$ --- equivalence holds iff the 90\% $t$-CI of the mean $\Delta $F1 lies entirely inside the margin (Schuirmann at $\alpha {=}.05$). Wilcoxon = two-sided exact signed-rank; $p^{\mathrm  {Holm}}$ = Holm-adjusted over the four split$\times $block comparisons. PASS/FAIL is the TOST verdict, not a significance claim: the random/graph FAIL is a CI entirely \emph  {below} zero (a directional centralized win on the leakage-prone split). \relax }}{5}{table.caption.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:stats}{{4}{5}{Corrected-baseline comparison (FedAvg $-$ strong centralized), paired per seed over 20 seeds, F1. \textbf {TOST}: pre-registered equivalence margin $\pm .02$ --- equivalence holds iff the 90\% $t$-CI of the mean $\Delta $F1 lies entirely inside the margin (Schuirmann at $\alpha {=}.05$). Wilcoxon = two-sided exact signed-rank; $p^{\mathrm {Holm}}$ = Holm-adjusted over the four split$\times $block comparisons. PASS/FAIL is the TOST verdict, not a significance claim: the random/graph FAIL is a CI entirely \emph {below} zero (a directional centralized win on the leakage-prone split). \relax }{table.caption.6}{}}
